Z||000000||80's BOY||04-05-2000||01:14 PM||||just got some pre-fabbed carpet from ACC. should i rip out the old carpet or go right over the existing carpet for a more quiet interior. i'm concerned about the thickness and weight of leaving in both layers. has anyone dealt with new Fiero carpeting before?? need some advice here in Texas.<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Alex4mula||04-05-2000||03:13 PM||||I did installed Mr. Mikes carpeting in my car. I don't know how yours looks but in my case it was about 1/4" thick. Mr. Mikes suggested installing it over the old one and so I did. Look was excellent. But i noticed that if it is more thick you may have some areas looking bulky , like the side of the center console. The original carpet has a thick molded rubber for sound deadning and soft feeling. If yours (new one) does not has it then install it on top of the old one. Otherwise you will end up driving like inside a coke can.||||reg||4
Z||000002||Spyder||04-05-2000||03:17 PM||||I'm taking my carpet out for the ACC brand. Some brands don't have the extra padding.<BR>I was more concerned with the smell left by the old carpet.<BR>I have done a trail fitting and it seems like it will fit fine with the old carpet removed.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||ezsurf||04-05-2000||06:16 PM||||I'd like to know more about ACC carpet.  Does ACC carpet have a padded backing?  Does it come with the door panels? Is ACC carpet better than Mr Mikes?  Where can I find ACC carpet?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||04-05-2000||08:19 PM||||I contacted Mr. Mikes about this a couple of months ago.  He said that the best way to do it is to peel the jute backing off of the new carpet then lay that over the original carpet.||||reg||1
Z||000005||pollock||04-06-2000||06:03 PM||||Do ACC and Mike offer the original style "salt and pepper" looking carpet?<BR>||||reg||1
